ut":"(1 + 2","expect":{}}],"docs":{},"source":"## Rational-friendly arithmetic: integer division that stays exact and\n## the operator soup around it. The tree keeps the operator captures\n## so the evaluator can pick per-operator semantics.\ngrammar Mathn version \"1.0.0\" {\n  ws = %x20 / %x09\n  pq = *ws\n  digit = %x30-39\n  number = 1*digit as number\n  primary = number / ( \"(\" pq expr pq \")\" )\n  term = primary *( pq ( \"*\" / \"/\" ) pq primary )\n  expr = term *( pq ( \"+\" / \"-\" ) pq term )\n  top = pq expr pq\n\n  entry main: top\n\n  test {\n    accept \"1 / 2\"\n    accept \"(1 + 2) / 3\"\n    accept \"4 * 2 - 1\"\n    reject \"/ 2\"\n    reject \"(1 + 2\"\n  }\n}\n","source_hash":"9e34a8b0fa7bdd003a16035ace0c638bd4089e65826482f79ba7642c8156377a","unicode_tables":"onigmo (Ruby 3.4.8)","compiler_version":"1.3.111","mode":"v2","emission":2,"checksum":"sha256:feffe4e155489e121da7facf0370c82ed59ef450212c7e0ae0a0cac6e48931e0"}
